<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
		App-level privacy manifest.

		NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes IS EMPTY, AND THAT IS A MEASURED RESULT, NOT A
		PLACEHOLDER.

		The required-reason API categories are UserDefaults (CA92.1), File
		Timestamp (C617.1), System Boot Time (35F9.1), Disk Space (E174.1) and
		Active Keyboards (3EC4.1). The complete iOS source that ends up in this
		binary is:

		  * ios/App/App/AppDelegate.swift  (the only first-party Swift file)
		  * node_modules/@capacitor/ios    (pods Capacitor + CapacitorCordova)
		  * node_modules/@capacitor/app/ios      (pod CapacitorApp)
		  * node_modules/@capacitor/browser/ios  (pod CapacitorBrowser)

		Those are exactly the four `pod` lines in ios/App/Podfile. Grepping that set for
		every symbol in the five categories (UserDefaults, NSUserDefaults,
		standardUserDefaults, creationDate, modificationDate,
		contentModificationDate, getattrlist*, stat/fstat/lstat,
		fileAttributes, attributesOfItem, systemUptime, mach_absolute_time,
		ProcessInfo, volumeAvailableCapacity*, systemFreeSize, statfs,
		activeInputModes) returns nothing. `npm run verify:ios` re-runs that scan
		against the installed dependency graph, so adding a pod that does use one
		of these APIs fails the check instead of shipping an undeclared reason.

		AppDelegate.swift uses FileManager.url(for:in:appropriateFor:create:),
		createDirectory and URL.setResourceValues(isExcludedFromBackup). None of
		those is a required-reason symbol: they neither read a file timestamp
		nor query free space.

		@capacitor/ios ships its own PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy inside each pod
		(Capacitor/Capacitor/PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy and
		CapacitorCordova/CapacitorCordova/PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy), both with empty
		NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes, which agrees with the scan.

		If a plugin is ever added, DO NOT copy a declaration from a blog post:
		re-run `npm run verify:ios`, read the pod's own manifest, and add only
		what the code proves.
	-->
	<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
	<array/>

	<!--
		No tracking. There is no analytics SDK, no advertising id, no attribution
		network and no third-party domain contacted from the app: the only
		network peer is the project's own Supabase instance, and EmoFlow emotion
		analysis is a deterministic local rule engine
		(src/lib/emotionCandidates.ts), not an external service.
	-->
	<key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
	<false/>
	<key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
	<array/>

	<!--
		Data the app collects, linked to the user's account and never used for
		tracking. This mirrors docs/privacy-access-matrix.md.

		  EmailAddress       sign-in identity (Supabase auth)
		  OtherUserContent   diary text, one-line records, schedule and trip
		                     notes, confirmed emotion tags
		  PhotosorVideos     record attachments in Supabase Storage
		  AudioData          voice records captured by MediaRecorder
		  Health             menstrual-cycle entries and settings
		                     (supabase/migrations/004_create_cycle_tables.sql);
		                     raw cycle rows are owner-only and are never shared
		                     with the partner

		All are NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposeAppFunctionality: the app cannot
		be a shared diary without storing what the user writes.
	-->
	<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
	<array>
		<dict>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeEmailAddress</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeLinked</key>
			<true/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeTracking</key>
			<false/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposes</key>
			<array>
				<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposeAppFunctionality</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeOtherUserContent</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeLinked</key>
			<true/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeTracking</key>
			<false/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposes</key>
			<array>
				<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposeAppFunctionality</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePhotosorVideos</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeLinked</key>
			<true/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeTracking</key>
			<false/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposes</key>
			<array>
				<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposeAppFunctionality</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeAudioData</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeLinked</key>
			<true/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeTracking</key>
			<false/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposes</key>
			<array>
				<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposeAppFunctionality</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeHealth</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeLinked</key>
			<true/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeTracking</key>
			<false/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposes</key>
			<array>
				<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposeAppFunctionality</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
